<t tx="sta.20261009033628.15">Two wikis, linked to each other. The pages are stored in this file.

In a page:
- gd on a [[link]] follows it; Ctrl-o comes back.
- [[ in INSERT offers the wiki's pages.
- Rename a page, such as North, and every link to it changes.

Commands:
- :export-wiki, on a page of @wiki garden, writes garden.md here.
- :check-wiki lists the pages that break a rule.
- :convert-wikilinks-to-unls rewrites the links for Python Leo.
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.16">A wiki about one vegetable garden. Start at [[Beds]].
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.17">Three beds: [[North]], [[South]] and [[Herbs|the herb bed]].

See also [[Watering]] and [[Sow\/transplant]].
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.18">Tomatoes and beans. Cover with [[glossary:Mulch]] in May.
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.19">Brassicas go here next year.
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.20">Squash.

A link in code is text: `[[North]]`.
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.21">Squash mildew in August. Water at the base.
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.22">Basil and thyme.
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.23">Every second day in summer. [[North]] dries first.

Two pages are headed Notes; a parent picks one: [[South/Notes]].

## Schedule

Morning, before 9.
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.24">Sow indoors in March, transplant in May.
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.25">Terms used in [[garden:]].
</t>
<t tx="sta.20261009033628.26">A layer over the soil that keeps it moist. Used on [[garden:Beds/North]].
</t>
</tnodes>
